  "explain": "<p>More than 90 percent (about 94 in e13): with scores of standard deviation 32, the best key usually beats the second by many units. With the scaling the favourite gets about 11 percent at every width, and the softmax's Jacobian is more than a hundred times larger for the typical query.</p>"
